- op: discuss  # edea
  at: '2026-08-28T05:44:22Z'  # edea
  by: agent  # edea
  actor: jgstern_agent  # edea
  clock: 3  # edea
  nonce: edea  # edea
  message: "DONE in PR #598 (dev, merged). Both halves shipped: the rows load, and the run\nsays so.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. python-http-clients.yaml and go-web-frameworks.yaml move out of\ndocs/ -- which pyproject.toml does not package, so an installed hypergumbo could\nnever read them and they shipped to NOBODY -- into\nhypergumbo_core/io_primitives_overlays/, declaring provenance: community and a\ndated retrieved:. Selected PER LANGUAGE (INV-lufib). hypergumbo-self.yaml stays\nin docs/: it is hypergumbo's OWN overlay for its own dependency set and carries\nmodule_completeness grants, which a default must never ship.\n\nTHE LOUD PART, which is the condition the ruling attaches. A run that loads\ncommunity rows prints per queried language the file, its retrieved date, where\nto override it and how to switch it off. Shaped after the in_progress warning\nand wired at the SAME THREE consumers, with a parity test that fails if the two\ndisclosures ever fire at different numbers of sites. catalog_provenance gains\n`shipped_default` as a THIRD state and the TEXT renderer emits it too -- a\ndisclosure that exists only under --json is half shipped (INV-karud a3), and\nhere it would also miss the ruling outright.\n\nTHE FINDING THAT CHANGED THE DESIGN, and it was live in my first cut. INV-buzab\nmakes \"the catalogue classified this call\" mean EXAMINED, and an examined call\nstops blocking a clean verdict. So shipping these rows plainly would have turned\n\"never writes to the host filesystem\" from inconclusive into CONFIRMED for every\nrepo using requests -- on the strength of rows describing only its NETWORK\nsurface. That is INV-zubuh (\"presence of SOME rows must not vouch for the rest\")\narriving through a new door, and it is the false-all-clear direction shipped by\ndefault to everyone. Caught by the existing control\ntest_the_third_party_module_still_blocks, not by review.\n\nTHE FIX IS AN ASYMMETRY: IoPrimitive gains `unvouched`, stamped AT MERGE so a\nfile cannot claim otherwise, and _uncatalogued_external_modules no longer treats\nan unvouched classification as examination. A community row ADDS detections --\nthat direction only ever adds findings -- and never licenses the all-clear.\nPinned with both directions, including a control that a vouched row (math, the\none module python.yaml flags complete) still DOES examine.\n\nTWO MORE GUARDS. A shipped default may not declare module_completeness, refused\nat load rather than reviewed at merge. And a default must not restate the\ncatalogue's stdlib claim: merge is self-over-argument with the overlay as\nreceiver, so without care python went provenance_declared -> in_progress the\nmoment defaults loaded, and every python run would have emitted \"results may be\nincomplete\" beside the true disclosure. A USER overlay's effect on status is\ndeliberately unchanged -- that is a separate question with its own measurement.\n\nFALLOUT HANDLED HONESTLY, not by weakening: 27 tests failed on the first run.\nPath moves aside, the premise tests now assert the STDLIB catalogue via\ninclude_defaults=False, which is what \"the built-in catalogue\" now spells, and\nADR-0047 ruling 1 keeps that rule exactly. The two taint-sink DELTA tests were\nre-based on a client hypergumbo does not ship, since a requests overlay no\nlonger adds anything. One test carried an explicit tripwire -- \"if this fails,\nADR-0016's scope decision needs revisiting rather than this test needing\nupdating\" -- and its docstring now records that the revisiting HAPPENED and was\nowner-accepted, rather than quietly flipping.\n\nAlso: --no-default-overlays on both consumers; io_primitives_overlays registered\nin YAML_CATALOGS (WI-tupid's gate caught the unregistered directory immediately)\nwith NO channel of its own, because a user's rows for this content belong in the\nio_primitives channel."  # edea
